# apps/web — frontend environment.
#
# The Next.js host is a thin client over the Python backend
# (apps/backend). All `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are baked into the
# browser bundle; do not put secrets here. Real auth happens via the
# Supabase JS client (docs/011 §3) using the publishable anon key,
# which is also public.

# The Python backend's HTTP base.
#
# Three sane values, depending on how you run:
#
#   ""                          (recommended) Use relative URLs so
#                               fetches stay same-origin through the
#                               Caddy proxy (.devcontainer/Caddyfile).
#                               Avoids CORS preflights entirely. This
#                               is the dev-container default since
#                               the proxy fronts everything on :3000.
#
#   http://localhost:8000       Cross-origin direct to FastAPI.
#                               Works (the backend's CORS allows
#                               localhost:3000) but each request
#                               pays a preflight. Useful when
#                               running the backend bare-metal.
#
#   https://api.example.com     Production same-origin (when the
#                               browser and API share a domain or
#                               you've fronted both with a CDN).
NEXT_PUBLIC_EIDAN_BACKEND_URL=
